% formalizes: claim:lib-9c
% claim: If a lost copy turns up, the replacement charge is cancelled and the fine stands
% says: If the copy turns up later, the replacement charge is cancelled and the fine stands.
% fidelity: strained — "cancelled" retracts a charge; Datalog cannot retract, so the charge is stated as not owed once the copy turns up, and the fine is untouched.
replacement_cancelled(L) :- lost(L), turned_up(L).
still_owes_replacement(M, C) :- owes_replacement(M, C), loan_copy(L, C), lost(L), not turned_up(L).
